comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T18:43:49.460Z",codex-agent,"Current PR deliberately performs zero dependent restores. Native close, auto-unblocking and warnings remain core-owned; only primary-only compensation can resume automatically. This follow-up owns the unique member compensation identity, complete domain and durable per-member checkpoints. The acceptance requires the full after-each-member SIGKILL matrix; the current pre-restore SIGKILL preservation tests are not claimed as that expanded recovery evidence. Pinned SDK remains the version adopted from main."
  "2026-11-02T09:18:34.227Z",pi-glm,"Triage 2026-11-02 (missed-watch sweep): still valid and correctly tracked here as the narrower member-progress subtask of gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#34's owner (pm-swarm-durable-close-recovery). PR #24 merged the reduced design (fresh native close only; journal replay refuses swarm_close_recovery_unsupported), so the durable per-member compensation/resume protocol this item owns remains undelivered. No duplicate item created."
  "2026-11-06T09:12:51.945Z",codex-sol,"Read the complete linked issues and current implementation. Verify the existing handoff successor guard with real processes; implement native-history-bound durable close intent and per-member recovery through the pinned SDK, with crash and peer-interleaving regressions. No SDK dependency bump or release workflow change planned."
  "2026-11-06T09:37:13.843Z",codex-sol,"First complete real-process SIGKILL matrix passed 57/57 tests: forward and reverse boundaries with one, two and three dependents, exact pre-close native bytes including timestamps, append-only audit streams and stable repeated recovery. The independent peer suite passed 14/14, including release/claim/restore ABA after every member decision and copied native identities between restores. Implementation persists immutable intent, post-close heads and restored progress in the registered swarm_close_intent field; no package journal files or SDK journal rewrites. Final gates and behavioral revert proofs remain pending."
  "2026-11-06T13:49:08.466Z",codex-sol,"The linked runner passes all one-to-three-dependent lost-return and lost-restore-progress scenarios with exact raw pre-close bytes and append-only native history. Copied phase markers cannot forge successful completion: the fresh invocation signs its full result; a real process killed after the primary commit reproduces the forged-result attack before the guard, and the guard revert fails. Related peer edits stop before compensation writes; final primary restore retains native dependent fences. Packed npm and Bun recovery passed all 24 member-boundary SIGKILL cases."
  "2026-11-14T09:01:50.027Z",codex-sweep-1114,"2026-11-14 sweep: returned idle or paused work to open; no agent is actively working this item. Delivered slices: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/65 merged 2026-11-11T09:10:50Z; merge SHA bb72f4fa6f2c30ab6b53a125aa3b1f0fc4f26b38; PR head 2378e884184d40299eede0b73f3ee276b9b0fae2. Delivered: Durable reverse compensation checkpoints every dependent member, recovers lost returns and SIGKILL boundaries, preserves peer edits and append-only history across packed npm/Bun consumers. Green at that head: test (22), codeql, test (26), CodeQL. Other check outcomes: enable-auto-merge: SKIPPED; cubic · AI code reviewer: NEUTRAL; CodeRabbit: SKIPPED; Sourcery review: SKIPPED (not counted as green). Linked GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/issues/32 is still OPEN; remaining: resolve and verify its outstanding acceptance before closure."
